# Each turn loads the key from the list and calls one stub with the map and the key in registers.
# LOOP-LABEL: loop #
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[key]] = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:indexedContiguousProperties, {{*}}:GetArrayElement)
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[found]] = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), b@[[key]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallInline)
# The answer comes back boxed. An integer and a double each take one test and one conversion; anything else is undefined, which travels as a marked NaN.
# LOOP: Int32 b@[[isInteger]] = AboveEqual(b@[[found]], b@{{*}}, {{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isInteger]], Terminal, {{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP: Double b@{{*}} = IToD(b@{{*}}, {{*}}:CallInline)
# The test of `??` is one comparison of the bits with the first marked NaN.
# LOOP: Int32 b@[[isMissing]] = GreaterEqual(b@{{*}}, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# LOOP-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isMissing]], Terminal, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# LOOP: Double b@{{*}} = Add(b@{{*}}, b@{{*}}, {{*}}:Add)
# LOOP-LABEL: end of loop
# The stub writes the storage of no array: the storage and the length of the list are loaded ahead of the loop.
# STORAGE-LABEL: loop #
# STORAGE-NOT: Reads:JSArray_butterfly
# STORAGE-NOT: Reads:Butterfly_publicLength
# STORAGE-LABEL: end of loop
# The stub is the only call of the loop.
# CALLS-LABEL: loop #
# A loop that calls is not cut into stretches of turns, so the loop polls on each of them.
# CALLS-COUNT-2: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-LABEL: end of loop
# Map.prototype.get cannot be replaced and nothing of the same name hides it on the object: the function does not read it by name, make its function object, or test the object or the function.
